    'body' => <<<'HTML'
<div class="key-takeaways"><h2>Key takeaways</h2><ul>
<li>A hail damage claim supplement asks the carrier to add missed, under-measured, mispriced, or newly discovered items to its estimate. It is a routine part of many roof claims.</li>
<li>Commonly missed items include starter, ridge cap, drip edge, flashing, pipe jacks and vents, waste, steep and high-roof labor, extra layers, decking found at tear-off, and soft metals.</li>
<li>Most carriers use Xactimate. A line-item estimate in the same format makes differences easy to see and discuss.</li>
<li>Every supplement item needs evidence: photos, measurements, manufacturer instructions or code requirements, and a short explanation.</li>
<li>Code-required work is paid only to the extent your policy covers it. No supplement is guaranteed to be approved.</li>
