<tr><td>Removal of additional layers</td><td>Layer count not checked</td><td>Photo of the roof edge or a cut showing each layer</td></tr>
<tr><td>Starter course</td><td>Treated as included in field shingles</td><td>Manufacturer installation instructions; eave and rake lengths</td></tr>
<tr><td>Ridge and hip cap</td><td>Left out or under-measured</td><td>Measured ridge and hip lengths, photos of the cap shingles</td></tr>
<tr><td>Drip edge</td><td>Not present on the old roof or overlooked</td><td>Photos of eaves and rakes; code and manufacturer requirements</td></tr>
<tr><td>Step and counter flashing</td><td>Assumed reusable</td><td>Photos of walls and chimneys; explanation of why it must be replaced to install new shingles correctly</td></tr>
<tr><td>Pipe jacks, vents, and caps</td><td>Soft metal damage not counted</td><td>Close-ups of each item with dents or cracks, with a count</td></tr>
<tr><td>Waste factor</td><td>Too low for roof complexity</td><td>Roof diagram showing hips, valleys, and cut-up areas</td></tr>
<tr><td>Steep and high-roof charges</td><td>Pitch or height not recorded</td><td>Pitch gauge photo; photos showing two-story eaves</td></tr>
<tr><td>Underlayment</td><td>Omitted or wrong type</td><td>Manufacturer requirements; code requirements for slope</td></tr>
<tr><td>Decking found at tear-off</td><td>Not visible at inspection</td><td>Photos before covering, measured sheet count, prompt notice to the carrier</td></tr>
<tr><td>Gutters, downspouts, screens</td><td>Separate trades, quickly reviewed</td><td>Photos of dents and tears, linear feet, counts</td></tr>
<tr><td>AC condenser fins</td><td>Treated as cosmetic</td><td>Close-up photos; an HVAC technician’s written assessment</td></tr>
<tr><td>Permit and code items</td><td>Not addressed in first pass</td><td>Permit requirement, code reference, and your ordinance or law coverage</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>

